course: dictionary
lesson: 936
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A blister is a small bubble under your skin, filled with clear liquid. «Breaking new boots in a little at a time, and changing wet socks at half-time, makes blisters less likely.» Here blisters means the sore bubbles that rubbing causes on your feet.
explain: Blister can also mean a bubble on paint or on a pie crust, and it can be a verb. «He did, and the burn blistered badly» uses the verb: the skin formed bubbles. Ask yourself: is this word a thing, or an action?
explain: Some phrases use blister in a picture-word way. «Blistering heat» means the heat is so strong it feels like it could blister your skin, so it means very hot. The context and the word around it tell you which meaning to choose.
fact: A blister is a small bubble under the skin, filled with clear liquid.
fact: Blisters are often caused by rubbing, such as from new shoes, or by a burn.
fact: If you get a blister, do not pop it: keep it clean and cover it with a plaster.
fact: «Blistering heat» means very hot.
fact: Blister can be a noun (a blister) or a verb (to blister, blistered, blistering).
exercise: «Breaking new boots in a little at a time makes blisters less likely.» What is a blister in this sentence? | A large lump of mud | A loud noise made by boots | A bubble on a pie crust | *A small bubble under the skin, filled with clear liquid
exercise: «The burn blistered badly.» What part of speech is blistered here? | An adjective meaning clean | *A verb, showing the skin formed bubbles | A noun meaning a shoe | A noun, the name of a plaster
exercise: Someone says «blistering heat». What does blistering mean? | Very cold | Very quiet | *Very hot | Very wet
test: «Tell a grown-up about a blister early and cover it with a plaster or blister pad.» What should you do with a blister? | Ignore it until it bursts | *Tell a grown-up and cover it | Pop it straight away | Put butter on it
test: «Poison ivy gives an itchy, blistering rash.» What does blistering mean here? | A new pair of shoes | A bubble on a pie crust | Very hot weather | *Causing small bubbles on the skin
exam: A boy in Leeds put butter on a burn, and the burn blistered badly. What does blistered mean here? | *Formed small bubbles on the skin | Was covered neatly with a plaster | Was cooled down with water | Healed in one day
